From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] os_install_service: Gentoo's cp tries FICLONE first

NickelOS Unified runs Gentoo's coreutils, whose cp asks for a reflink clone
(ioctl FICLONE) before copying; ext4 refuses it and cp copies. This policy
allowed ioctl for listed requests only, so cp was killed while the
installer copied the stateful partition. With it allowed, an install from
inside the sandbox completes and the installed disk boots.

---
--- a/conf/os_install_service-seccomp-amd64.policy
+++ b/conf/os_install_service-seccomp-amd64.policy
@@ -14,7 +14,9 @@
 # CDROM_LAST_WRITTEN = 0x5395
 # FS_IOC_FIEMAP = 0xc020660b
 # BLKGETZONESZ = 0x80041284
-ioctl: arg1 == BLKALIGNOFF || arg1 == BLKDISCARD || \
+# NickelOS Unified: Gentoo's coreutils cp first tries to clone a file (FICLONE,
+# 0x40049409; ext4 refuses and cp copies).
+ioctl: arg1 == 0x40049409 || arg1 == BLKALIGNOFF || arg1 == BLKDISCARD || \
        arg1 == BLKDISCARDZEROES || arg1 == BLKGETSIZE64 || \
        arg1 == BLKIOMIN || arg1 == BLKIOOPT || arg1 == BLKPBSZGET || \
        arg1 == BLKROGET || arg1 == BLKRRPART || arg1 == BLKFLSBUF || \
